      "title": "The master policy and the certificate",
      "narration": "Priya signs the group health contract for her bakery. That document is the master policy, and Priya, the employer, is the policyholder. Her employees are not parties to the contract. Each covered employee receives a certificate of coverage, sometimes called a certificate of insurance or evidence of coverage, describing the benefits, exclusions, cost sharing and how to file a claim. The certificate is a summary; the master policy controls if they differ. Dependents are covered through the employee’s certificate. When a question asks who the insured is in group coverage, the answer is the employee; who owns the policy, the employer.",
