      "title": "What the certificate must say",
      "narration": "Because the certificate is all most employees ever see, Maryland and federal law require it to be accurate and complete. It must describe the benefits and limitations, the conditions for eligibility, how coverage ends and the continuation and conversion rights that follow. Maryland’s continuation statutes specifically require each certificate to explain how a surviving spouse, a divorced spouse or a terminated employee may elect continued coverage. The Affordable Care Act added the summary of benefits and coverage, a standardized four-page comparison document. A certificate that misstates benefits exposes the insurer to claims for the benefits described.",
