      "title": "Experience and community rating",
      "narration": "How is the group’s premium set? Experience rating bases next year’s premium on this group’s own claims history, adjusted for trend and expenses; it is used for large groups whose claims are statistically credible. Community rating charges all groups in an area the same rate regardless of claims. Federal and Maryland law now require modified community rating for small employers: premiums may vary only by age within a 3 to 1 band, tobacco use, geographic rating area and family composition, never by the group’s health or claims. Priya’s twenty-person bakery is community rated; a 2,000-employee hospital is experience rated.",
