      "title": "Why only true groups",
      "narration": "Group insurance works because the group formed for some purpose other than buying insurance. Employees come together to work, union members to bargain, borrowers to borrow. That natural purpose means the group’s health is roughly average and no one joined because they were sick. A group assembled solely to buy insurance would attract the people who most need it, defeating the pricing. State laws therefore define the eligible groups, require a minimum size in some cases, and in Maryland permit true small employers down to a single eligible employee through the small group market and SHOP.",
